From 309501010f4dbfbb03e2540031cd2cdf30b5abdd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 21 May 2026 20:37:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: Phase 11 patch 0074 -- Bug 6 ship fix: RATEDIV
 auto-default + SB16 CT1745 mixer balance

Why DOS needs this:

The consolidated Bug 6 ship fix, building on 0073's rate instrumentation.
Two parts, pure SDL.

PART 1 -- RATEDIV auto-default (bakes the proven Tier-2 fix):

The bug6-confirm iter (0073 rate-diag) MEASURED device->spec.freq = 44100
in ALL tiers: the SB16 opens at 44100 regardless of the Tier-2
SAMPLE_RATE=11025, which only sets the Pixtone MASTER render rate. The
IRQ-5 ISR consumes the master at the device frame rate (one int16 per
output stereo pair = 44100/s) while the master represents only
master_int16_rate int16/s, so Tier-2 SFX play 4x too fast (2 octaves);
RATEDIV=4 corrects (operator-confirmed). The earlier "2x chip over-drain"
guess was overturned by the measurement.

0074 makes the divider automatic + tier-aware:
  - New export SDL_DOSPixtoneSetMasterRate(int master_int16_rate),
    declared in include/SDL3/SDL_dospixtone.h (single source of truth for
    the cross-link-unit symbol; mirrored into SDL_dos_audio_synth.h),
    implemented in sb.c. The engine (nxengine-evo, separate patch) calls
    it with SAMPLE_RATE*AUDIO_CHANNELS in SoundManager::init BEFORE
    MIX_CreateMixerDevice.
  - At OpenDevice (after SDL_UpdatedAudioDeviceFormat finalizes
    device->spec.freq, at the 0073 rate-diag site), cache dev_freq +
    resolve the env override + recompute the ISR shift:
    divider = round(device->spec.freq / master_rate); shift_div = ctz(d)
    for power-of-2 d (Tier-2 44100/11025=4 -> 2; Tier-1 44100/44100=1 ->
    0); non-power-of-2 -> nearest power of 2 + a warning. The
    SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_PIXTONE_IRQ_RATEDIV env knob (0073) is now a DEBUG
    OVERRIDE that wins when set ("1"/"2"/"4").
  - The 0073 RATEDIV env-resolve is RELOCATED out of the 0071 Lever-3
    hint block (which runs before the spec is finalized) to the rate-diag
    site where device->spec.freq is final. A shared recompute helper is
    also called from the setter for late-call safety; the env override
    always wins; whoever runs last produces the final shift.
  - Banner: "audio: SDL/0074 RATEDIV auto: dev_freq=%d master_rate=%d
    divider=%d shift_div=%d (env override=%s)".
  - master_rate / dev_freq / env_shift are NOT ISR-read (only the
    resulting Uint8 shift is, already DPMI-locked from 0073), so they
    need no DPMI lock.

PART 2 -- SB16 CT1745 analog mixer balance lever (NEW):

After the pitch fix the last Bug-6 blocker was SFX too quiet vs OPL3
music even at digital full-scale -- the SFX cannot be boosted digitally
without clipping. Root cause: the SB16 driver only ever programmed the
DSP rate + DMA (+ the SB Pro 0x0E stereo bit on the pre-SB16 path),
never the CT1745 analog mixer, so the PCM(Voice/SFX)-vs-FM(music) balance
sat at the card power-on default which favors FM. The fix is analog
(no digital clip risk):

  - In the is_sb16 OpenDevice path, after the 0xB6 DMA-mode setup,
    program the CT1745 volume registers (mixer_addr=base+0x04,
    data=base+0x05; 5-bit level in bits 7-3, value = level<<3):
      Master 0x30/0x31 = 31<<3 (max -- deterministic reference state)
      Voice  0x32/0x33 = voice_vol<<3  (PCM/DAC = the SFX path)
      FM     0x34/0x35 = fm_vol<<3     (OPL3 music)
  - Env knobs (cache-at-boot, decimal, clamp 0..31):
    SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_SB16_VOICE_VOL (default 31),
    SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_SB16_FM_VOL (default 24 -- lowers music for the
    balance). Killswitch SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_SB16_MIXER_PROGRAM strict-"0"
    -> touch nothing (byte-identical to pre-0074); default = program.
  - Banner: "audio: SDL/0074 SB16 mixer balance: master=31 voice=%d
    fm=%d (...)" or the DISABLED variant.
  - CT1745-specific so scoped to is_sb16; pre-SB16 cards keep current
    behavior.

Byte-identity: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_SB16_MIXER_PROGRAM=0 -> the CT1745 block
is skipped -> mixer untouched == pre-0074. The auto-RATEDIV ship default
is intentionally NOT byte-identical to pre-0074 (it bakes RATEDIV=4 for
Tier-2); the byte-identical fallbacks are MIXER_PROGRAM=0 (mixer) and
Lever-3-off OR PIXTONE_IRQ_RATEDIV=1 (divider).

0073's rate-diag + rate-meas instrumentation is kept intact. The smoke
BANNER_REGEX gets the RATEDIV-auto + SB16-balance banners (the superseded
0073 RATEDIV banner regex is repurposed); the 3 new env vars are
documented in docs/internal/BOOT.md.

DOSBox-X smoke confirms the banners / boot path but NOT the audible pitch
or balance per [[dosbox_not_proxy]]; both validate only on real DX2-66
hardware (the SB16 balance-sweep verify iter dials in voice/fm).

Cross-link-unit: SDL_DOSPixtoneSetMasterRate is engine->SDL (defined in
libSDL3.a, called from the engine), so it adds no unresolved extern to
the SDL test exes. Signature locked with nx-engine: int arg, C linkage,
declared in the public header that the engine #includes.

Workspace-local per memory/sdl_ai_policy.md; never upstreamed.

See docs/internal/BUG6-BALANCE-AND-SHIP-FIX-DESIGN.md (flush-instr spec)
+ bug6_sfx_clip_pitch_mechanism + v1_0_1_rc2_iter_verdict.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>
